{
 "about": "Complex creatures (复杂造物) run by graphs, a first try in the game: scene_add_creature_skill, scene_set_creature_logic and the three kinds of creature graph. A scout is ordered about through custom variables (walk to x 12, work, walk back to x 0, stroll); an archer is given an enemy as its target and shoots. What to look for in the prints: BR_AT shows the scout's x going from 2 to 12 after BR_ORDER 0 and back to 0 after BR_ORDER 2; BR_SIGNAL work after BR_ORDER 1; BR_SIGNAL shoot after BR_FOE. BR_CALL shows that a creature's own server graph hears its skill (whenSkillNodeIsCalled). The level's navigation mesh is baked before the playtest (bakeNavigation): without it the scout does not stroll. Since 2026-10-14 the signal BR_work carries three values from the scout's skill graph (a client graph) to the server, an integer, a vector and a string, declared with defineSignal in both graphs: the log shows BR_SIGNAL work 3 {1.0,2.5,-3.0} dig.",
